.TH TWEEN_START 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
tween_start \- Animate *target from its current value to `to` over duration seconds using ease (NULL = linear)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqtween.h\(dq
.BI "void tween_start(Tween *tw, float *target, float to, float duration, EaseFn ease);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Animate *target from its current value to `to` over duration seconds using ease (NULL = linear). target must stay valid for the tween's life (a scene static or GameState field, never a local). Starting a tween that is already running restarts it from the current value, which makes retargeting smooth. A duration of 0 completes on the next update.
.SH MODULE
tween (src/engine/tween/tween.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tween_update (3),
.BR tween_done (3),
.BR Tween (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
